  "observations": [
    "Whole-branch foliage follows the retained large-tree cards and all four inspected small-tree card layouts without atlas repacking. Front and rear views retain transparent silhouette gaps.",
    "The near and middle underside caps sample the authored endgrain patch. Their trunk side islands do not intersect it. The middle cap visibly stretches its rings with the retained low-detail geometry.",
    "The distant tree keeps original bark because its side UVs intersect the entire endgrain patch. Small-tree bark also remains original in these comparisons.",
    "At the matched 3840 by 2160 view, 512px keeps the small-tree outline and leaf groups readable; 1024px retains finer leaf and twig edges. This is a visual staging comparison, not a final preset or performance measurement.",
    "Brighter leaf groups and the pale bark remain candidates for review with actual material normals, lighting and tint. Repeated branch fans and close cut-end stretching require game art review."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "No original game geometry or full original images are included in the public evidence. Capture hashes identify retained local review files.",
    "No normal-map, game shader, wind, unhealthy sapling tint, growth, weather or LOD-transition acceptance.",
    "The imported fourth small-beech mesh has no gameplay-prefab join established in this review.",
    "UV review is scoped to these slots and views; no whole shared-material approval, runtime binding or final art approval."
  ]
